+/// GNX-PROP: reads what a prop does on one event (arg0) into a struct; arg1 = who, arg2 = the key (for
+/// mod errors), arg3 = frames of the prop's sprite. Every part is optional and they add up:
+///   frame  jump to this frame (0 = the first)          step  move this many frames at once (-64..64)
+///   play   run this many frames forward (1-999) at react.speed, or "next_stop": up to the next of the
+///          react block's stops (after the last stop: to the end of the strip, then frame 0)
+///   flash  seconds of a flash fading out (0.05-10), or { "time": s, "color": c, "alpha": 0-1 }
