+/// GNX-PROP: reads a prop's "react" block (arg0) into one struct; arg1 = who (for mod errors), arg2 = the
+/// frames of the prop's sprite. The prop listens to the cell on one side of its passage:
+///   side    "left", "right", "both" (default) or "facing" (right, left while the prop is mirrored;
+///           draw the PNG facing right)
+///   speed   frames per second of "play" (0.1-60, default 8)
+///   at_end  "loop" (default: after the last frame comes the first) or "hold" (stays on the last frame;
+///           a step back below the first frame stays on the first)
+///   stops   frames where "play": "next_stop" stops: a list [3, 6, 9] or { "every": 3, "until": 60 }
+///           (3, 6 ... 60); after the last stop a play runs to the end of the strip and on to frame 0
+///   on      { "event": { what to do } }, events in gnx_react_events(), actions in gnx_react_action_parse
+/// Returns undefined when nothing usable is in it.
